From cd48856f0add3a4677519b924f08efd23166f059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evan <kirtzevan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:10:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix RLPx implementation so it completes a real handshake
 and Hello exchange

Verified end-to-end against @ethereumjs/devp2p as the listening peer.

- keccak: round-constant table was corrupted and the pi step was transposed,
  so every hash was wrong; add incremental API for the running frame MACs
- ecies: HMAC input must be iv || ciphertext || shared-mac-data
- handshake: EIP-8 auth body is rlp[sig, pubk, nonce, 4] + random padding
  (no ephemeral hash), raw recovery id, keep raw auth/ack packets
- secrets: egress/ingress MACs are keccak states seeded with
  (mac-secret ^ nonce) || packet; AES-256-CTR streams are per-direction
  and continuous across frames
- framing: rewritten per spec (16-byte encrypted header + header MAC,
  16-byte padded body + frame MAC via AES-ECB(mac-secret) seeding)
- add p2p Hello/Disconnect/Ping/Pong, snappy codec, enode/hex key parsing,
  hostname resolution, recv timeouts, `make test`, key generation script
- stop printing private keys and shared secrets to stdout

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015T3rS29gR18bxCjuU5uCSo
